dhārtarāṣṭrān sa-bāndhavān
sva-janaṁ hi kathaṁ hatvā
sukhinaḥ syāma mādhava\"}]},{\"section\":\"synonyms\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.synonyms\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"books.Synonyms\",\"title\":\"synonyms\",\"id\":373,\"bb\":341,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/1/36/b341/\",\"shadow_value\":\"pāpam – vices; eva – certainly; āśrayet – must come upon; asmān – us; hatvā – by killing; etān – all these; ātatāyinaḥ – aggressors; tasmāt – therefore; na – never; arhāḥ – deserving; vayam – we; hantum – to kill; dhārtarāṣṭrān – the sons of Dhṛtarāṣṭra; sa-bāndhavān – along with friends; sva-janam – kinsmen; hi – certainly; katham – how; hatvā – by killing; sukhinaḥ – happy; syāma – will we become; mādhava – O Kṛṣṇa, husband of the goddess of fortune.\",\"word_for_word_value\":[{\"word\":\"pāpam\",\"translation\":\"vices\"},{\"word\":\"eva\",\"translation\":\"certainly\"},{\"word\":\"āśrayet\",\"translation\":\"must come upon\"},{\"word\":\"asmān\",\"translation\":\"us\"},{\"word\":\"hatvā\",\"translation\":\"by killing\"},{\"word\":\"etān\",\"translation\":\"all these\"},{\"word\":\"ātatāyinaḥ\",\"translation\":\"aggressors\"},{\"word\":\"tasmāt\",\"translation\":\"therefore\"},{\"word\":\"na\",\"translation\":\"never\"},{\"word\":\"arhāḥ\",\"translation\":\"deserving\"},{\"word\":\"vayam\",\"translation\":\"we\"},{\"word\":\"hantum\",\"translation\":\"to kill\"},{\"word\":\"dhārtarāṣṭrān\",\"translation\":\"the sons of Dhṛtarāṣṭra\"},{\"word\":\"sa-bāndhavān\",\"translation\":\"along with friends\"},{\"word\":\"sva-janam\",\"translation\":\"kinsmen\"},{\"word\":\"hi\",\"translation\":\"certainly\"},{\"word\":\"katham\",\"translation\":\"how\"},{\"word\":\"hatvā\",\"translation\":\"by killing\"},{\"word\":\"sukhinaḥ\",\"translation\":\"happy\"},{\"word\":\"syāma\",\"translation\":\"will we become\"},{\"word\":\"mādhava\",\"translation\":\"O Kṛṣṇa, husband of the goddess of fortune\"}]}]},{\"section\":\"translation\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.translation\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"translation\",\"id\":374,\"bb\":342,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/1/36/b342/\",\"body_value\":\"Sin will overcome us if we slay such aggressors. Therefore it is not proper for us to kill the sons of Dhṛtarāṣṭra and our friends. What should we gain, O Kṛṣṇa, husband of the goddess of fortune, and how could we be happy by killing our own kinsmen?\"}]},{\"section\":\"purport\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.purport\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":375,\"bb\":343,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/1/36/b343/\",\"body_value\":\"$25\"}]}],\"short_title\":\"Bg. 1.36\",\"medium_title\":\"Bhagavad-gītā As It Is 1.36\"},\"locale\":\"en\",\"activeView\":\"$6:props:activeView\"}]}],\"$L26\",\"$L27\",\"$L28\"]}]\n"])self.__next_f.push([1,"2a:I[83068,[\"/_next/static/chunks/130enlymdm.jk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0b6f_zxj9ay~6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/143cg6c13uly6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07vk.k35-e~ti.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0j6k6n9cniknh.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0.zxv9arc6a56.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/00-zmo-3n1bt8.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0p4z5tusn0jt6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/01mcazkjru_is.js\"],\"default\"]\n30:I[78455,[\"/_next/static/chunks/130enlymdm.jk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0b6f_zxj9ay~6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/143cg6c13uly6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07vk.k35-e~ti.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0j6k6n9cniknh.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0.zxv9arc6a56.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/00-zmo-3n1bt8.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0p4z5tusn0jt6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/01mcazkjru_is.js\"],\"default\"]\n26:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-4 w-full max-w-screen-xl mx-auto md:px-8 mb-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"nav\",null,{\"aria-label\":\"Breadcrumb\",\"className\":\"breadcrumb mb-8 text-base\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"ol\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"/en/library/\",{\"className\":\"inline\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L20\",null,{\"href\":\"/en/library/\",\"className\":\"text-vb-link\",\"children\":\"Libr